  "coupon": "The published feature-fitted middle/fine/finer local predictions keep both cut faces clamped at a 2.7 mm half-span, nominal 1 mm crown, 0.6 mm shaft. Both signed force branches, plus a common 1 N preload, are explicitly recorded.",
  "common_guide": "A nonlinear 96 mm shell drives eight finite web/steel contact patches. Middle 0.055 mm2 shell / 2112-node local patch and fine 0.025 mm2 / 6528-node patch. Pure bends and four saved 500 g end conditions. Unmodified shell checkpoint reactions are verified against the pin-seat archive.",
